                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-08T12:00:00-03:00">March 8,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. My telegram No. 95, the Debt Service Decree was signed by the President at
                    00:30 this morning. It will be released for publication here and abroad
                    tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Department’s No. 58, March 7, 7 p.m., Aranha has changed his statement to conform
                    to the Department’s wishes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
